# Engine safety rules

## Before changing a function
- Read the WHOLE function and every caller (`rg -n "function_name\(" --type py`). Many functions return
  sentinel values that callers branch on: `RemoteListing.ok`, `sync_folder` → subtree-complete bool,
  `sync_subpath` → `None` or `"cold"`, `delete_orphans` → `(n_deleted, n_failed)`, `upload_batch` → bool.
- Keep the existing design comments. They record production incidents. If your change invalidates
  a comment, update the comment in the same commit.

## Stable output tags are an API
`[upload-failed]`, `[auth-failed]`, `[account-changed]`, `[subpath-cold]`, `[subpath-cold-root]`,
`[subpath-excluded]`, `@@PROGRESS`, `📂 <path>` lines, and any tag a plan adds (e.g. `[run-result]`).
The GUI and the consumer parse them. Never translate them, rename them, or move them inside `_()`.
Add new tags, don't repurpose old ones.

## Cache (`Cache` class, `~/.proton-drive-sync/…/*.cache`)
- Entry format `{"sig": {...}, "delete_synced": bool, "subtree_complete": bool}` plus legacy bare-signature
  entries and the reserved `"__meta__"` key. Readers must keep accepting all three.
- Changing the shape of `_local_signature()` invalidates EVERY cached directory and forces a full
  remote re-listing on the next pass (hours on big trees). Do not do that unless the plan says so.
  Store new per-file data in new entry fields instead.
- The cache is a shortcut, never proof of remote state. Only write a cache entry after the folder's
  uploads AND deletions fully succeeded (`had_failure == False`).

## Uploads
- Any "does this file need uploading?" decision must go through one comparator (`needs_upload`, or
  its successor named in the plan). Do not add ad-hoc size checks elsewhere.
- When information is missing (no remote size, no remote digest, unreadable local file), choose the
  conservative answer: upload, or report a failure. Never "assume unchanged".

## Deletions
- Three gates must all pass: master `--delete` flag, mapping `allow_delete`, mount guard (`_delete_guard_ok`).
  Never weaken a gate. Never delete when a listing failed (`RemoteListing.ok == False`).
- `remote_trash` only trashes. Do not reintroduce permanent deletion.
- Any new deletion path needs a dry-run print, a log line, and a test with the fake CLI.

## Real-time consumer
- Markers are acknowledged (`_cleanup`) only after the engine reports success for that subpath.
- Every non-success path must restore markers AND be rate-limited (no engine relaunch every cycle on a
  persistent error).

## systemd units (`schedule_manager.build_service_text`)
- A persistent error must never cause a tight restart loop. Use `SuccessExitStatus` /
  `RestartPreventExitStatus` deliberately and test the generated text.
- Paths in `ExecStart=` must be quoted/escaped for systemd (spaces, `%` → `%%`, quotes).
